																		Re: Site Criticism Team - Staff Review
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rurascarlet" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5287847); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5287847&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349838" alt="RuraScarlet" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5287847)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rurascarlet" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5287847); return false;" >RuraScarlet</a></span> <span class="odate time_1575510185 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">05 Dec 2019 01:43</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4438532">
									

<p>Thank you so much for the critique! I will gladly implement this in my future works.</p>
<p>As to my character choice, Bright is very much a comfort character to me, and I wasn't strong enough emotionally to write it from my own perspective so I needed to move the narrative away from myself to make something that's actually passable, thus making this a Bright tale.</p>
<p>I am getting professional help too, if you worry for me, which, don't, I'm okay, really. A talk with a psychiatrist isn't the same as organic interaction, though, and I just recently realized how alone I really was without the latter. I'm glad that I have a few on site people that I talk to sometimes, but it's just&#8230;different. than having friends to hang out with. Not that it's bad! No, just different. It was just the lack of people to confide to when I was in a dark place that hit me most and pushed me to make this.</p>
<p>This quickly became a second vent so I'll stop it here. Thank you so much for giving me advice, and, thank you again, for being someone out there who cares.</p>

							</div>

								
					
